# Copy to .env.local for development, and set the same variable in the Vercel
# project settings for production. .env* is gitignored; this example file is not.

# Google Maps Embed API key, used by the map on /contact.
#
# OPTIONAL. Without it the map still renders, via an undocumented keyless Google
# URL that works today but is not a supported API. Set this to move onto the
# real Maps Embed API — the component switches over on its own.
#
# To create one:
#   1. Google Cloud console -> APIs & Services -> enable "Maps Embed API".
#   2. Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key.
#   3. Restrict it, which matters because NEXT_PUBLIC_ keys ship to the browser:
#        - Application restrictions: HTTP referrers
#            https://redpear.vercel.app/*
#            http://localhost:3000/*
#        - API restrictions: Maps Embed API only
#
# Maps Embed API "place" mode is free and unmetered, but an unrestricted key can
# be lifted from the page and used against your other enabled APIs.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
